{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: RNA-only, PCA, singleprofile → 48.5% acc), the most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality carries useful signal for this task. Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) provides a clean, single-variable test: it holds profile setting constant (singleprofile) and swaps the modality from RNA to image, using a standard pretrained encoder. If image features yield substantially higher accuracy, it strongly motivates exploring the multimodal branch (configs 016–051) and justifies budget there. If image features perform comparably or worse, it indicates the bottleneck is representation quality within a single modality, redirecting budget toward better RNA encoders (scvi, scgpt) or multiprofile aggregation. This experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the single highest-level design decision (modality contribution) before committing budget to more complex fusion/aggregation choices."
}

